cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cited for the 14-day maximum validity constraint on certificates
  cited in serverCertificateHashes, which the Chromium implementation
  enforces at the QUIC handshake layer."
title: "WebTransport"
type: standard
authors:
  - name: "W3C WebTransport Working Group"
url: "https://www.w3.org/TR/webtransport/"
notes: "The serverCertificateHashes bypass to normal WebPKI requires the
  cited certificate to (a) use ECDSA over P-256, (b) sign with
  ecdsa-with-SHA256, (c) carry a validity period no longer than 14 days.
  Chromium enforces the constraints in QuicTransportClientSession /
  QuicWebTransportSession. RFD 2145 sets the WebTransport leaf row's
  notAfter at exactly 14 days; RFD 2144 documents the Bao PKI mount
  (pki-wt/) whose role produces certs at that ceiling."
